# =============================================================================
# VM Pool Manager — SERVICE image dependencies  (SOURCE / documentation only)
# =============================================================================
#
# NOTE: These deps are a STRICT SUBSET of proxy/requirements.in (fastapi, uvicorn,
# httpx, boto3, psycopg2-binary). In the shared local .venv they are installed via
# the merged, hash-pinned proxy/requirements.txt lock — this file is NOT compiled
# or installed on its own and there is deliberately no pool_manager/requirements.txt
# lockfile. It is passed as a compile INPUT (to document coverage) and kept as the
# minimal source-of-truth for what the pool-manager SERVICE container needs. See
# proxy/requirements.in for the lock-regeneration command.
# =============================================================================
#
# This is the runtime dependency set for the pool-manager SERVICE container
# image (pool_manager/Dockerfile), the same process local_install.sh starts
# bound to POOL_BIND_HOST (127.0.0.1 by default; the container binds 0.0.0.0).
#
# It is DISTINCT from the other two requirement sets in this repo:
#   • proxy/requirements.txt  — the full proxy host deps (AI/agent, data catalog,
#                               encryption, formatting). The pool manager needs
#                               NONE of that: no strands-agents, bedrock-agentcore,
#                               pandas, pyarrow, onnx, scikit-learn, joblib, ruff,
#                               sqlglot, cryptography, websockets. Those are proxy /
#                               AI / data-catalog concerns, not pool-manager runtime.
#   • app/requirements.txt    — the IN-VM (Firecracker) app deps. Unrelated.
#
# Derived by reading what pool_manager/*.py and proxy/storage/*.py actually import
# on the pool manager's code paths. Keep this MINIMAL — add a line only when an
# import on a reachable path needs it.
#
# Pins are >= ranges, the same style as proxy/requirements.in.

# Web framework — pool_manager/server.py (FastAPI app + uvicorn entrypoint)
fastapi>=0.139.0
uvicorn>=0.51.0

# HTTP client — pool_manager/aws_backend.py (VM /health, /rebind, /restore-state)
httpx>=0.28.1

# AWS SDK — pool_manager/aws_backend.py (boto3 'lambda-microvms' control-plane client)
boto3>=1.43.51

# PostgreSQL driver — REQUIRED. The pool manager hard-imports proxy.storage, and in
# ECS it runs with STORAGE_BACKEND=postgres against the shared Aurora pool_vms ledger.
# proxy/storage/postgres_db.py imports psycopg2 lazily in initialize() and raises a
# RuntimeError if the driver is absent, so without this line the pool-manager service
# cannot reach the shared ledger at all. proxy/requirements.txt carries the same
# driver + pin for the proxy's own Postgres path (both services share proxy.storage).
psycopg2-binary>=2.9
